{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"c046fc46-a04e-4eff-8713-886146b7feff","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Start with a right triangle. Its perpendicular sides measure three and four; the side opposite the right angle is the hypotenuse.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Pythagorean theorem"},{"op":"figure","id":"squares","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-4.7,7.7],"y":[-3.7,7.7],"axes":"none","equal_scale":true},"marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"a","at":[0,0]},{"kind":"point","id":"b","at":[3,0]},{"kind":"point","id":"c","at":[0,4]},{"kind":"polyline","points":[{"at":"a"},{"at":"b"},{"at":"c"}],"closed":true},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"a"},"from":{"at":"b"},"to":{"at":"c"}},{"kind":"text","at":[1.5,0.35],"text":"3"},{"kind":"text","at":[0.35,2],"text":"4"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"c046fc46-a04e-4eff-8713-886146b7feff","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Build a square on each perpendicular side. Their areas are nine and sixteen square units.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"leg_squares","on":"squares","marks":[{"kind":"polyline","points":[{"at":"a"},[0,-3],[3,-3],{"at":"b"}],"closed":true,"fill":true},{"kind":"polyline","points":[{"at":"a"},{"at":"c"},[-4,4],[-4,0]],"closed":true,"fill":true},{"kind":"text","at":[1.5,-1.5],"text":"9"},{"kind":"text","at":[-2,2],"text":"16"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"leg_areas","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"3^2+4^2=9+16=25"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"c046fc46-a04e-4eff-8713-886146b7feff","step":{"id":"s3","script":"The square on the hypotenuse has exactly their combined area. So its area is twenty-five, and the hypotenuse measures five.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"hyp_square","on":"squares","marks":[{"kind":"polyline","points":[{"at":"b"},[7,3],[4,7],{"at":"c"}],"closed":true,"fill":true},{"kind":"text","at":[3.5,3.5],"text":"25"},{"kind":"text","at":[1.2,1.7],"text":"5"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"theorem","anchor":{"el":"leg_areas","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"a^2+b^2=c^2"},{"op":"equation","id":"hyp_length","anchor":{"el":"theorem","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"c=\\sqrt{25}=5"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Which square's area equals the sum of the other two areas?","expected_gist":"The square on the hypotenuse."}}}
